[12.345748, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' docs/METHOD.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.347074, "o", "# How we compute daily ET0\r\n\r\nThis is the method the `et0` package must follow. It is the daily FAO-56 Penman-Monteith procedure: FAO Irrigation\r\nand Drainage Paper No. 56, *Crop evapotranspiration* (Allen, Pereira, Raes and Smith, 1998), chapters 3 and 4.\r\nEquation numbers below are the book's, so you can look any step up there. You do not need the book: everything the\r\npipeline needs is on this page.\r\n\r\nET0 is the water a well-watered reference grass surface would lose in one day, in mm/day. We publish one value per\r\nstation per day.\r\n\r\n## 1. Inputs, after conversion to standard form\r\n\r\n"]
[12.347118, "o", "| Symbol | Meaning | Unit |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Tmax, Tmin | daily maximum and minimum air temperature | deg C |\r\n| u2 | mean daily wind speed **at 2 m above ground** | m/s |\r\n| Rs | incoming solar radiation, daily total | MJ m-2 day-1 |\r\n| ea | actual vapour pressure | kPa |\r\n| J | day of the year: 1 on 1 January, up to 365 (366 in a leap year) | - |\r\n| latitude | decimal degrees, **north positive, south negative** | deg |\r\n| z | station elevation above sea level | m |\r\n\r\nStation records do not always arrive in this form. Section 3 lists every form our station register and raw files use\r\nand how each one is converted. The FAO-56 equations themselves (section 2) only ever see the standard form.\r\n\r\n## 2. The daily procedure\r\n\r\nConstants: solar constant Gsc = 0.0820 MJ m-2 min-1; Stefan-Boltzmann constant sigma = 4.903e-9 MJ K-4 m-2 day-1;\r\nalbedo of the reference grass 0.23; absolute temperature in Eq. 39 is T + 273.16.\r\n\r\n"]
[12.347156, "o", "1. Mean temperature (Eq. 9): Tmean = (Tmax + Tmin) / 2.\r\n2. Air pressure from elevation (Eq. 7): P = 101.3 * ((293 - 0.0065 z) / 293) ^ 5.26, in kPa.\r\n3. Psychrometric constant (Eq. 8): gamma = 0.665e-3 * P, in kPa/degC.\r\n4. Saturation vapour pressure at temperature T (Eq. 11): e0(T) = 0.6108 * exp(17.27 T / (T + 237.3)), in kPa.\r\n5. Mean saturation vapour pressure (Eq. 12): es = (e0(Tmax) + e0(Tmin)) / 2. Do not use e0(Tmean) here.\r\n6. Slope of the saturation curve at Tmean (Eq. 13): Delta = 4098 * e0(Tmean) / (Tmean + 237.3)^2, in kPa/degC.\r\n7. Actual vapour pressure ea, from whichever humidity the station reports (section 3.5):\r\n   - from daily maximum and minimum relative humidity (Eq. 17): ea = [e0(Tmin) RHmax/100 + e0(Tmax) RHmin/100] / 2;\r\n   - from the daily mean dewpoint temperature (Eq. 14): ea = e0(Tdew).\r\n8. Extraterrestrial radiation Ra (Eqs. 21 to 25), with phi = latitude in radians (Eq. 22, negative in the south):\r\n   - inverse relative Earth-Sun distance (Eq. 23): dr = 1 + 0.033 cos(2 pi J / 3"]
[12.347183, "o", "65);\r\n   - solar declination (Eq. 24): delta = 0.409 sin(2 pi J / 365 - 1.39), in radians;\r\n   - sunset hour angle (Eq. 25): ws = arccos(-tan(phi) tan(delta)), in radians;\r\n   - Ra = (24 * 60 / pi) * Gsc * dr * [ws sin(phi) sin(delta) + cos(phi) cos(delta) sin(ws)] (Eq. 21), MJ m-2 day-1.\r\n   The divisor is 365 in every year, leap years included; J itself runs to 366 in a leap year.\r\n9. Clear-sky radiation (Eq. 37): Rso = (0.75 + 2e-5 z) * Ra.\r\n10. Net shortwave radiation (Eq. 38): Rns = (1 - 0.23) * Rs.\r\n11. Net longwave radiation (Eq. 39):\r\n    Rnl = sigma * [(Tmax + 273.16)^4 + (Tmin + 273.16)^4] / 2 * (0.34 - 0.14 sqrt(ea)) * (1.35 Rs/Rso - 0.35),\r\n    where the ratio Rs/Rso is limited to at most 1.0 before it is used.\r\n12. Net radiation (Eq. 40): Rn = Rns - Rnl.\r\n13. Soil heat flux for a daily step (Eq. 42): G = 0.\r\n14. Reference evapotranspiration (Eq. 6):"]
[12.347204, "o", "\r\n    ET0 = [0.408 Delta (Rn - G) + gamma * 900 / (Tmean + 273) * u2 * (es - ea)] / [Delta + gamma (1 + 0.34 u2)],\r\n    in mm/day. The factor 0.408 turns MJ m-2 day-1 into mm/day of evaporated water (Eq. 20).\r\n\r\n`et0/fao56.py` implements steps 1 to 14, and `python -m et0.selfcheck` checks it against the daily worked example in\r\nchapter 4 of the book (Example 18, ET0 = 3.88 mm/day).\r\n\r\n"]
[12.347233, "o", "## 3. Station register and raw files\r\n\r\n### 3.1 The register (`config/stations.yaml`)\r\nA YAML file with a list `stations`. Every station has every key below; there are no other forms than the ones listed.\r\n\r\n| Key | What it holds |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `id` | station code; the raw file is `<data folder>/<id>.csv` |\r\n| `name`, `network` | free text, not used in the calculation |\r\n| `latitude` | see 3.2 |\r\n"]
[12.34727, "o", "| `longitude` | decimal degrees, east positive; not used by the daily method |\r\n| `elevation_m` | elevation above sea level in metres (z in Eqs. 7 and 37) |\r\n| `wind_height_m` | height of the anemometer above ground in metres; see 3.3 |\r\n| `radiation_units` | unit of the `solar_rad` column; see 3.4 |\r\n| `humidity` | which humidity columns the raw file has; see 3.5 |\r\n\r\n### 3.2 Latitude\r\nTwo forms are used:\r\n- a number: signed decimal degrees, north positive, south negative (`38.42`, `-31.85`);\r\n- text: unsigned decimal degrees followed directly by the hemisphere letter `N` or `S` (`\"36.95N\"`, `\"34.92S\"`).\r\n  `\"34.92S\"` is the same place as `-34.92`.\r\n\r\n### 3.3 Wind sensor height\r\n`wind_ms` is the mean daily wind speed at the anemometer, which may be at any height (any positive value of"]
[12.347298, "o", "\r\n`wind_height_m` between 1 m and 20 m; 2, 3 and 10 m are the most common). The equations need u2, the speed at 2 m.\r\nConvert with the logarithmic wind profile (Eq. 47), for every station:\r\n\r\n    u2 = uz * 4.87 / ln(67.8 z_w - 5.42)\r\n\r\nwhere uz is the measured speed and z_w the anemometer height in metres. At 10 m the factor is about 0.748; at 2 m it is\r\n1.000 (to three decimals).\r\n\r\n### 3.4 Radiation units\r\n- `MJ/m2/day`: daily total incoming solar radiation, already Rs.\r\n"]
[12.347321, "o", "- `W/m2`: daily mean solar irradiance. Multiply by 0.0864 to get Rs in MJ m-2 day-1 (1 W m-2 sustained for a day is\r\n  86 400 J m-2 = 0.0864 MJ m-2).\r\n\r\n### 3.5 Humidity\r\n- `rh_minmax`: columns `rh_max_pct` and `rh_min_pct` (daily maximum and minimum relative humidity, %); use Eq. 17.\r\n- `dewpoint`: column `tdew_c` (daily mean dewpoint temperature, deg C); use Eq. 14.\r\n\r\n### 3.6 Raw daily files (`<data folder>/<id>.csv`)\r\n"]
[12.347353, "o", "One row per day, no gaps and no missing values. Columns: `date` (YYYY-MM-DD), `tmax_c`, `tmin_c`, the humidity\r\ncolumn(s) of 3.5, `wind_ms` (m/s at the anemometer height), `solar_rad` (in the station's `radiation_units`).\r\n\r\n## 4. Output\r\nCSV with a header row and the columns `station_id`, `date` (YYYY-MM-DD) and `et0_mm_day`: one row for every station\r\nand every day in the input. The pipeline writes three decimals.\r\n"]
[12.3476, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@84a2b8c5-0934-41d4-b383-0acd7a467647:/app# "]
[15.26627, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' et0/fao56.py\n"]
[15.266413, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' et0/fao56.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[15.26797, "o", "\"\"\"FAO-56 Penman-Monteith reference evapotranspiration, daily time step.\r\n\r\nImplements the daily procedure of FAO Irrigation and Drainage Paper 56 (Allen et al., 1998), chapters 3 and 4, as\r\nwritten up in /app/docs/METHOD.md. Every function works on numpy arrays (one element per day).\r\n\r\nInputs expected by et0_daily (already in standard form):\r\n    tmax, tmin   daily maximum and minimum air temperature [deg C]\r\n    u2           mean daily wind speed at 2 m above ground [m/s]\r\n"]
[15.268018, "o", "    rs           incoming solar radiation [MJ m-2 day-1]\r\n    ea           actual vapour pressure [kPa] (see actual_vapour_pressure_*)\r\n    doy          day of the year, 1 = 1 January\r\n    latitude     decimal degrees, north positive, south negative\r\n    elevation    metres above sea level\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\nSOLAR_CONSTANT = 0.0820        # MJ m-2 min-1\r\nSTEFAN_BOLTZMANN = 4.903e-9    # MJ K-4 m-2 day-1\r\nALBEDO = 0.23                  # hypothetical grass reference\r\n\r\n"]
[15.268044, "o", "\r\ndef atmospheric_pressure(elevation):\r\n    \"\"\"Eq. 7, kPa.\"\"\"\r\n    return 101.3 * ((293.0 - 0.0065 * np.asarray(elevation, float)) / 293.0) ** 5.26\r\n\r\n\r\ndef psychrometric_constant(pressure):\r\n    \"\"\"Eq. 8, kPa/degC.\"\"\"\r\n    return 0.665e-3 * pressure\r\n\r\n\r\ndef saturation_vapour_pressure(t):\r\n    \"\"\"Eq. 11, kPa.\"\"\"\r\n    t = np.asarray(t, float)\r\n    return 0.6108 * np.exp(17.27 * t / (t + 237.3))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef vapour_pressure_slope(t):\r\n    \"\"\"Eq. 13, kPa/degC.\"\"\"\r\n"]
[15.268072, "o", "    t = np.asarray(t, float)\r\n    return 4098.0 * saturation_vapour_pressure(t) / (t + 237.3) ** 2\r\n\r\n\r\ndef actual_vapour_pressure_rh(tmax, tmin, rh_max, rh_min):\r\n    \"\"\"Eq. 17, kPa, from daily maximum and minimum relative humidity [%].\"\"\"\r\n    return (saturation_vapour_pressure(tmin) * np.asarray(rh_max, float) / 100.0\r\n            + saturation_vapour_pressure(tmax) * np.asarray(rh_min, float) / 100.0) / 2.0\r\n\r\n\r\ndef actual_vapour_pressure_dewpoint(tdew):\r\n"]
[15.26809, "o", "    \"\"\"Eq. 14, kPa, from the daily mean dewpoint temperature [degC].\"\"\"\r\n    return saturation_vapour_pressure(tdew)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef extraterrestrial_radiation(latitude, doy):\r\n    \"\"\"Eqs. 21-25: Ra [MJ m-2 day-1] and the sunset hour angle ws [rad].\"\"\"\r\n    phi = np.deg2rad(np.asarray(latitude, float))\r\n    doy = np.asarray(doy, float)\r\n    dr = 1.0 + 0.033 * np.cos(2.0 * np.pi * doy / 365.0)\r\n    decl = 0.409 * np.sin(2.0 * np.pi * doy / 365.0 - 1.39)\r\n    ws = np.arccos(np.clip(-np.tan(phi) * np.tan(decl), -1.0, 1.0))\r\n    ra = (24.0 * 60.0 / np.pi) * SOLAR_CONSTANT * dr * (\r\n        ws * np.sin(phi) * np.sin(decl) + np.cos(phi) * np.cos(decl) * np.sin(ws))\r\n    return ra, ws\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[15.268107, "o", "def daylight_hours(ws):\r\n    \"\"\"Eq. 34, hours.\"\"\"\r\n    return 24.0 / np.pi * ws\r\n\r\n\r\ndef clear_sky_radiation(ra, elevation):\r\n    \"\"\"Eq. 37, MJ m-2 day-1.\"\"\"\r\n    return (0.75 + 2e-5 * np.asarray(elevation, float)) * ra"]
[15.268129, "o", "\r\n\r\n\r\ndef net_longwave_radiation(tmax, tmin, ea, rs, rso):\r\n    \"\"\"Eq. 39, MJ m-2 day-1. Rs/Rso is limited to 1.0.\"\"\"\r\n    rel = np.minimum(np.asarray(rs, float) / rso, 1.0)\r\n    tk4 = ((np.asarray(tmax, float) + 273.16) ** 4 + (np.asarray(tmin, float) + 273.16) ** 4) / 2.0\r\n    return STEFAN_BOLTZMANN * tk4 * (0.34 - 0.14 * np.sqrt(ea)) * (1.35 * rel - 0.35)\r\n\r\n"]
[15.268152, "o", "\r\ndef et0_daily(tmax, tmin, u2, rs, ea, doy, latitude, elevation):\r\n    \"\"\"Eq. 6, FAO-56 Penman-Monteith reference evapotranspiration [mm/day]; soil heat flux G = 0 (Eq. 42).\"\"\"\r\n    tmax = np.asarray(tmax, float)\r\n    tmin = np.asarray(tmin, float)\r\n    u2 = np.asarray(u2, float)\r\n    rs = np.asarray(rs, float)\r\n    ea = np.asarray(ea, float)\r\n    tmean = (tmax + tmin) / 2.0\r\n"]
[15.268168, "o", "    delta = vapour_pressure_slope(tmean)\r\n    gamma = psychrometric_constant(atmospheric_pressure(elevation))\r\n    es = (saturation_vapour_pressure(tmax) + saturation_vapour_pressure(tmin)) / 2.0\r\n    ra, _ = extraterrestrial_radiation(latitude, doy)\r\n    rso = clear_sky_radiation(ra, elevation)\r\n    rns = (1.0 - ALBEDO) * rs\r\n    rnl = net_longwave_radiation(tmax, tmin, ea, rs, rso)\r\n    rn = rns - rnl\r\n    g = 0.0\r\n    num = 0.408 * delta * (rn - g) + gamma * (900.0 / (tmean + 273.0)) * u2 * (es - ea)\r\n    den = delta + gamma * (1.0 + 0.34 * u2)\r\n"]
[15.26818, "o", "    return num / den\r\n"]
[15.268417, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[15.268434, "o", "root@84a2b8c5-0934-41d4-b383-0acd7a467647:/app# "]
[19.154394, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' et0/ingest.py\n"]
[19.263957, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' et0/ingest.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\"\"\"Read one station's raw daily file and turn it into the standard daily inputs used by fao56.et0_daily.\"\"\"\r\nimport os\r\n\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\n\r\nfrom . import fao56\r\n\r\nBASE_COLUMNS = [\"date\", \"tmax_c\", \"tmin_c\", \"wind_ms\", \"solar_rad\"]\r\nHUMIDITY_COLUMNS = {\"rh_minmax\": [\"rh_max_pct\", \"rh_min_pct\"], \"dewpoint\": [\"tdew_c\"]}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_station(station, data_dir):\r\n    \"\"\"Return a DataFrame with columns station_id, date, doy, tmax, tmin, ea, u2, rs (standard units).\"\"\"\r\n    path = os.path.join(data_dir, f\"{station.station_id}.csv\")\r\n    raw = pd.read_csv(path)\r\n    if station.humidity not in HUMIDITY_COLUMNS:\r\n        raise ValueError(f\"{station.station_id}: unknown humidity type {station.humidity!r}\")\r\n    missing = [c for c in BASE_COLUMNS + HUMIDITY_COLUMNS[station.humidity] if c not in raw.columns]\r\n    if missing:\r\n        raise ValueError(f\"{path}: missing columns {missing}\")\r\n\r\n    dates = pd.to_datetime(raw[\"date\"], format=\"%Y-%m-%d\")\r\n    df = pd.DataFrame({\r\n  "]
[19.263995, "o", "      \"station_id\": station.station_id,\r\n        \"date\": dates.dt.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\"),\r\n        \"doy\": dates.dt.dayofyear.astype(int),\r\n        \"tmax\": raw[\"tmax_c\"].astype(float),\r\n        \"tmin\": raw[\"tmin_c\"].astype(float),\r\n    })\r\n    if station.humidity == \"dewpoint\":\r\n        df[\"ea\"] = fao56.actual_vapour_pressure_dewpoint(raw[\"tdew_c\"].astype(float))\r\n    else:\r\n        df[\"ea\"] = fao56.actual_vapour_pressure_rh(df[\"tmax\"], df[\"tmin\"], raw[\"rh_max_pct\"].astype(float),\r\n                                                   raw[\"rh_min_pct\"].astype(float))\r\n    df[\"u2\"] = raw[\"wind_ms\"].astype(float)          # m/s at 2 m\r\n    df[\"rs\"] = raw[\"solar_rad\"].astype(float)        # MJ m-2 day-1\r\n    return df\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@84a2b8c5-0934-41d4-b383-0acd7a467647:/app# "]
[30.548767, "i", "apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: et0/ingest.py\n@@\n-import os\n-\n-import pandas as pd\n-\n-from . import fao56\n+import os\n+import numpy as np\n+\n+import pandas as pd\n+\n+from . import fao56\n@@\n-    df[\"u2\"] = raw[\"wind_ms\"].astype(float)          # m/s at 2 m\n-    df[\"rs\"] = raw[\"solar_rad\"].astype(float)        # MJ m-2 day-1\n+    # Convert wind speed from the anemometer height to the standard 2 m height.\n+    # Equation 47 from FAO‑56: u2 = uz * 4.87 / ln(67.8 * z_w - 5.42)\n+    # `station.wind_height_m` is guaranteed to be present (1‑20 m).\n+    uz = raw[\"wind_ms\"].astype(float)\n+    z_w = float(station.wind_height_m)\n+    # Guard against division by zero or invalid log argument.\n+    if z_w <= 0:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"{station.station_id}: invalid wind sensor height {z_w}\")\n+    u2 = uz * 4.87 / np.log(67.8 * z_w - 5.42)\n+    df[\"u2\"] = u2\n+\n+    # Convert solar radiation to MJ m‑2 day‑1 if necessary.\n+    rs_raw = raw[\"solar_rad\"].astype(float)\n+    # The register sp"]
[30.548887, "i", "ecifies the units; accept \"MJ/m2/day\" (or similar) as already in MJ.\n+    rad_units = getattr(station, \"radiation_units\", \"MJ/m2/day\").lower()\n+    if rad_units in [\"w/m2\", \"w/m^2\", \"w/m2/day\", \"w/m^2/day\"]:\n+        # Convert from W m‑2 (mean daily irradiance) to MJ m‑2 day‑1.\n+        df[\"rs\"] = rs_raw * 0.0864\n+    else:\n+        # Assume the value is already in MJ m‑2 day‑1.\n+        df[\"rs\"] = rs_raw\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n"]
[30.548934, "o", "apply_patch <<'PATCH'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
